Block 206 does not license item 1 to be renamed as item 2. The primary runner
must expose every function argument and dependency edge between these objects.
A phase label, momentum, coframe, port, or orbit index is not eta.

## Stage B: native action factorization

Rebuild the two nonzero H1 off-diagonal TT vertices from the native centered
cosine, centered-difference, creation, and annihilation factors. Prove by exact
Laurent equality whether the 110-term effective source is generated by a
finite composition of radius-one action factors in both the literal forward
and actual reverse directions. Report the dependency DAG, maximum microstep
depth, support after each multiplication, and any factor that already requires
non-nearest-neighbor data.

A positive algebraic factorization is not yet a physical M2 compiler. It must
be reported separately from a map that consumes actual one-site conditions.

## Stage C: decoder-selection discriminator

Reconstruct independently the two-dimensional proper-cubic Hom space from a
conditional six-site Bloch-vector shell to the H1 T2 shear. Let D_o and D_e be
the odd-shell and even-shell basis maps. Determine whether the frozen action
factorization supplies any equation that fixes one law-level pair (a,b) in
D=a D_o+b D_e before the TT shear is supplied.

Positive closure requires:

- an explicitly typed internal cubic action on M2 derived from existing
  physical data rather than supplied as a coframe;
- one fixed decoder, not coefficients fitted to the H1 output;
- exact reconstruction of both source directions on all 24 frames;
- identical eta never demanding inequivalent sources or probabilities;
- no global p, q, port, orbit lookup, or source-location label; and
- the inherited nonconstant positive binary law without changing its state or
  effect family.

As a deliberately overgenerous falsifier only, encode Block 206's six phase
conditions as simultaneous equatorial Bloch vectors and enumerate every
proper-cubic internal frame. This comparator cannot establish closure because
its input is not an inherited six-Record state. It can falsify a claim that
the visible phase pattern uniquely selects the decoder.

